{"kind":"report","text":"Changes requested on exact 48b1fee9a1071f3fa4afed62025c470acc160c10 for row-write accounting request #8900 (git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:8bd623cc41cf18c9189bb6e716b56431edc18d10).\n\nP2 — Keep the measurement switch from worsening ordinary pin scheduling. packages/room/src/core.ts@48b1fee9a1071f3fa4afed62025c470acc160c10:1469–1471 builds arrays for every pending pin and spreads them into Math.min. nextAlarm calls it through loopPendingKinds and again at line 1979, even when PIN_DELAY_MS is unset. In a real Durable Object, 5,000 pending pins cause 10,000 pin-query rowsRead per nextAlarm versus 5,000 on landed safe-error code; at 150,000 retained pending pins, loopPendingKinds throws RangeError: Maximum call stack size exceeded. Both controls pass on the landed baseline and fail on this candidate. The old one(...) helper also materializes all matching rows, so this is a doubled scan, not a claimed regression from one row. Preserve a cheap default-off path, avoid unbounded argument spreading and duplicate scans, and add backlog controls for the ordinary path and delayed-pin scheduling. Reproduction source: /tmp/artroom-checker-rows-v3-pin-default-control.test.ts; final paired logs: /tmp/artroom-checker-rows-v3-pin-default-{candidate,landed}.log.\n\nRepair on current main df22d7713cc239f96a92f74596ee87509967a99f, preserving the safe-error recovery and scrub scheduling just landed by receipt git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f58aad79d3d720dbbe6f5e5279ea6b100e3576fb. core.ts and room.ts overlap. Keep the pin/mint earliest-due, per-kind backoff, repository-gone fences and unfounded scrub/founding progress together, with composed tests, then republish the exact artifact set for review. This verdict authorizes no merge.\n\nThe prior accounting defects are repaired: all nine retained independent controls pass, including malformed billed fields, namespace pagination, provider-message redaction, start-stamped storage samples, exact invocation windows, redaction before truncation, and malformed owned namespaces. The four previously absent isolated measurements now have saved windows and billing samples. Offline recomputation confirms pending-pin 2 written/136 read (including the switch, with the report's explicit unresolved split), empty tick 0/202, check windows 17 writes twice, and activation paired write differences [2,20,16] at N=0 and [32,31,37] at N=3. These remain measurement estimates and upper bounds as qualified, not universal costs. Saved invocation rows are absent, so their per-minute columns cannot be independently reconstructed. The 120-second storage lookback is an explicit provider-interval assumption, not a proved maximum.\n\nTidy the summaries in the same repair: not every quiet window wrote zero—the first check's before-control wrote 2; the clean smoke's 1,270 includes 1,258 across its three Rooms plus 12 in Registry. Keep check raw-window reads distinct from baseline-adjusted estimates. The detailed tables already make those distinctions recoverable. git diff --check also reports three new blank lines at EOF (deploy notes, main cost report, checks.test.ts).\n\nArchitecture: this changes application measurement tooling, deployment configuration and Room scheduling (gitseq layers 5–7 and host-facing application integration); it does not alter the Git, kernel or nexus contracts. The P2 violates the intended default-off behavior and scalability. The new declared-acts direction #10285 explicitly lets lanes already under review finish; these code-review measurements do not establish a fixed platform act vocabulary.\n\nSecurity: the spike-only operator decision #9651 (git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:66a41558f53c0e1baf5abdcb6cec8074b5bc3a29) remains effective and authorizes no production setting. No config enables it. Accounting errors fail closed, and the repaired output path redacts known credentials before bounding. Retained backlog availability is unresolved. I used synthetic credentials, fake provider responses and local Durable Objects only; no deployment, provider billing query, credential creation or live deletion was performed for this review.\n\nSimplification: calculate the needed pin due time once, use a bounded/existence path when the switch is off, and keep the measurement conclusions consistent across summaries. Preserve complete functionality; no schedule-based reduction is requested. Future lane-C publication costs and budget enforcement remain explicitly outstanding, not silently counted as delivered.\n\nIndependent validation in clean disposable clones: npm ci, root npm test and npm run typecheck exit 0; root counts are checkers 43, CLI 162, client 88+2, Git 285, log 198+193, MCP 73+5, policy 199+198 (one skipped), Room 232+475, UI 141. Room Wrangler 4.146.0 deploy --dry-run exits 0 without uploading. Twenty-nine accounting mutations and nine pin mutations each produce a named runtime test failure, not a parse/load failure; sources restored and 56 focused Node plus 8 pin Durable Object tests pass. Mutation evidence is under /tmp/artroom-checker-rows-v3-mut and /tmp/artroom-checker-rows-v3-pin-mut. Both review checkouts are clean.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:9cda251c10aa9c583d167c8927e3fae0f9e669ea","binding":"assigned","head":"48b1fee9a1071f3fa4afed62025c470acc160c10","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:f6e0e317d333c7d0deed3d1f417dbea6b1a7b52f\"]","implementations":"[\"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:7f3d305c3d4defed39ac3e9c9b8f7326e239fba7\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aaf3#git:sha1:b2cdc44a4fd2967f4ecd6a366dfa67df36f513b8","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"changes-requested"}}